============================================================
SEQUENCES
============================================================

n:         [3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
m:         [1, 3, 6, 10, 15]

P(n) = nonzero multilinear coefficients:
  [2, 6, 35, 200, 1782]

Σ H = sum over all 2^m tilings:
  [4, 32, 632, 29696, 3251200]

2^m · E[H] = Σ H (integer!):
  [4, 32, 632, 29696, 3251200]

E[H] = mean Hamiltonian paths with fixed base path:
  [2.0, 4.0, 9.875, 29.0, 99.21875]

max H (= A038375 for global max):
  [3, 5, 15, 45, 189]

Distinct H values:
  [2, 3, 7, 19, 77]

E_lin(n) = 1 + Σ (n-s)·2^(s-2):
  E_lin(3) = 2
  E_lin(4) = 5
  E_lin(5) = 12
  E_lin(6) = 27
  E_lin(7) = 58
  E_lin(8) = 121
  E_lin(9) = 248
  E_lin(10) = 503
  E_lin(11) = 1014
  E_lin(12) = 2037
  E_lin(13) = 4084
  E_lin(14) = 8179

Σ H counts (tiling, HP) pairs = |{(t, σ) : σ is HP of T(t)}|
  This equals: Σ_σ 2^(m - |tiles constrained by σ|)
  = Σ_σ 2^(m - (n-1) + (base path arcs used by σ))
  = Σ_σ 2^(C(n-1,2) - n + 1 + bp(σ))
  where bp(σ) = number of base-path arcs used by σ.
  n=3: Σ H = 4 = 2 × 2^1 + 0
  n=4: Σ H = 32 = 4 × 2^3 + 0
  n=5: Σ H = 632 = 9 × 2^6 + 56
  n=6: Σ H = 29696 = 29 × 2^10 + 0
  n=7: Σ H = 3251200 = 99 × 2^15 + 7168

